1
00:00:49,930 --> 00:00:52,930
And give her a teaspoon of the medicine after every meal.

2
00:00:52,930 --> 00:00:54,930
Don't worry. She'll be fine.

3
00:00:54,930 --> 00:00:58,930
You're welcome. Good-bye.

4
00:00:58,930 --> 00:01:11,930
How are you?

5
00:01:11,930 --> 00:01:13,930
I'm tired and hungry.

6
00:01:13,930 --> 00:01:15,930
Well, Marilyn and Richard called.

7
00:01:15,930 --> 00:01:17,930
They'll be here soon, and then we'll eat.

8
00:01:17,930 --> 00:01:20,930
All right. Is...is Susan coming?

9
00:01:20,930 --> 00:01:22,930
Well, she'll be here later.

10
00:01:22,930 --> 00:01:24,930
She has to work late tonight.

11
00:01:24,930 --> 00:01:25,930
And what's Robbie cooking for dinner? Robbie

12
00:01:25,930 --> 00:01:28,930
It's a surprise.

13
00:01:28,930 --> 00:01:31,930
I hope it's pasta.

14
00:01:31,930 --> 00:01:38,930
Robbie, the dinner was terrific. Robbie

15
00:01:38,930 --> 00:01:40,930
Yes, it was delicious.

16
00:01:40,930 --> 00:01:43,930
What's for dessert?

17
00:01:43,930 --> 00:01:45,930
Oh, I forgot dessert.

18
00:01:45,930 --> 00:01:48,930
Robbie! Robbie

19
00:01:48,930 --> 00:01:49,930
Don't worry.

20
00:01:49,930 --> 00:01:51,930
We've got lots of ice cream.

21
00:01:51,930 --> 00:01:53,930
Oh, I'd love some ice cream.

22
00:01:53,930 --> 00:01:59,930
Well, there's chocolate and coffee and a little vanilla.

23
00:01:59,930 --> 00:02:00,930
I'll have vanilla.

24
00:02:00,930 --> 00:02:02,930
Is that all right with everyone?

25
00:02:02,930 --> 00:02:03,930
I'll have chocolate.

26
00:02:03,930 --> 00:02:05,930
Me, too.

27
00:02:05,930 --> 00:02:08,930
Uh, one scoop of coffee

28
00:02:08,930 --> 00:02:10,930
and one scoop of chocolate for me.

29
00:02:10,930 --> 00:02:14,930
Robbie, will you help me serve? Robbie

30
00:02:14,930 --> 00:02:27,930
I keep thinking about that bag of film. Eight rolls.

31
00:02:27,930 --> 00:02:31,930
A whole day's work.

32
00:02:31,930 --> 00:02:33,930
And good stuff, too.

33
00:02:33,930 --> 00:02:35,930
Don't worry, Richard.

34
00:02:35,930 --> 00:02:36,930
Somenoe will find it.

35
00:02:36,930 --> 00:02:42,930
I'll get it. Hello.

36
00:02:42,930 --> 00:02:49,930
Hello.

37
00:02:49,930 --> 00:02:52,930
Does Richard Stewart live here? Richard Stewart

38
00:02:52,930 --> 00:02:54,930
Yes, he's my brother.

39
00:02:54,930 --> 00:02:56,930
I'm Robbie...Robbie Stewart.

40
00:02:56,930 --> 00:02:59,930
I'm Alexandra Pappas.

41
00:02:59,930 --> 00:03:00,930
How do you do?

42
00:03:00,930 --> 00:03:04,930
Your brother left his bag of film on the ferryboat.

43
00:03:04,930 --> 00:03:05,930
I found it.

44
00:03:05,930 --> 00:03:07,930
I'm really glad to see you.

45
00:03:07,930 --> 00:03:10,930
I mean...my brother'll be really glad to see you!

46
00:03:10,930 --> 00:03:12,930
Robbie! Who is it? Robbie

47
00:03:12,930 --> 00:03:15,930
It's Richard's film! Richard

48
00:03:15,930 --> 00:03:18,930
I mean, Alexandra Pappas.

49
00:03:18,930 --> 00:03:20,930
Come in, please.

50
00:03:20,930 --> 00:03:27,930
Alexandra! Alexandra

51
00:03:27,930 --> 00:03:29,930
Hello, Richard. I found your bag!

52
00:03:29,930 --> 00:03:32,930
Oh, thank you! Thank you!

53
00:03:32,930 --> 00:03:34,930
Um...Alexandra, let me introduce you.

54
00:03:34,930 --> 00:03:36,930
This is my wife Marilyn.

55
00:03:36,930 --> 00:03:38,930
Richard showed me your photo. Richard

56
00:03:38,930 --> 00:03:39,930
How do you do?

57
00:03:39,930 --> 00:03:40,930
Oh yes.

58
00:03:40,930 --> 00:03:41,930
Richard told us all about you. Richard

59
00:03:41,930 --> 00:03:43,930
It's nice to meet you.

60
00:03:43,930 --> 00:03:45,930
And this is my mother, Ellen Stewart.

61
00:03:45,930 --> 00:03:46,930
How do you do?

62
00:03:46,930 --> 00:03:48,930
And my father, Dr. Philip Stewart.

63
00:03:48,930 --> 00:03:50,930
Nice to meet you, Alexandra.

64
00:03:50,930 --> 00:03:51,930
And...ah...you met Robbie.

65
00:03:51,930 --> 00:03:54,930
Yes. And you must be Susan. Hi.

66
00:03:54,930 --> 00:03:56,930
Hi. Welcome.

67
00:03:56,930 --> 00:03:58,930
I'm so glad you found the bag

68
00:03:58,930 --> 00:04:01,930
and took the time and trouble to return it.

69
00:04:01,930 --> 00:04:02,930
Oh, it was no trouble.

70
00:04:02,930 --> 00:04:04,930
I just took the wrong train.

71
00:04:04,930 --> 00:04:06,930
Would you like something to eat?

72
00:04:06,930 --> 00:04:07,930
Thank you, no.

73
00:04:07,930 --> 00:04:09,930
I'm late for dinner at my house.

74
00:04:09,930 --> 00:04:10,930
I really have to go.

75
00:04:10,930 --> 00:04:12,930
Would you like to call home?

76
00:04:12,930 --> 00:04:13,930
I'd appreciate that.

77
00:04:13,930 --> 00:04:15,930
Please, use the phone.

78
00:04:15,930 --> 00:04:17,930
Thanks. Excuse me.

79
00:04:17,930 --> 00:04:21,930
Alexandra's a high-school exchange student from Greece. Alexandra

80
00:04:21,930 --> 00:04:22,930
Where does she live?

81
00:04:22,930 --> 00:04:24,930
With a family in the Bronx.

82
00:04:24,930 --> 00:04:26,930
Oh, that's not too far from here!

83
00:04:26,930 --> 00:04:28,930
Take it easy, Robbie.

84
00:04:28,930 --> 00:04:30,930
Thank you.

85
00:04:30,930 --> 00:04:32,930
I can only stay a few minutes.

86
00:04:32,930 --> 00:04:35,930
Have some iced tea.

87
00:04:35,930 --> 00:04:37,930
Thanks, Mrs. Stewart.

88
00:04:37,930 --> 00:04:40,930
Please sit down, Alexandra.

89
00:04:40,930 --> 00:04:49,930
So, you're an exchange student.

90
00:04:49,930 --> 00:04:50,930
Where do you go to school?

91
00:04:50,930 --> 00:04:53,930
At the Bronx High School of Science.

92
00:04:53,930 --> 00:04:55,930
Oh, that's a very good school.

93
00:04:55,930 --> 00:04:57,930
What are your favorite subjects?

94
00:04:57,930 --> 00:04:59,930
Biology and mathematics.

95
00:04:59,930 --> 00:05:01,930
Richard tells me you're a doctor. Richard

96
00:05:01,930 --> 00:05:03,930
Yes, a pediatrician.

97
00:05:03,930 --> 00:05:05,930
And what does your father do?

98
00:05:05,930 --> 00:05:08,930
He's a lawyer, in Thessaloniki.

99
00:05:08,930 --> 00:05:09,930
Would you like some pasta?

100
00:05:09,930 --> 00:05:11,930
I made it myself.

101
00:05:11,930 --> 00:05:12,930
It might be a little cold.

102
00:05:12,930 --> 00:05:17,930
Thanks, no. I do have to go.

103
00:05:17,930 --> 00:05:19,930
It was nice meeting you all.

104
00:05:19,930 --> 00:05:21,930
Well, maybe you'll come for lunch some Sunday,

105
00:05:21,930 --> 00:05:23,930
so we can really thank you

106
00:05:23,930 --> 00:05:24,930
for bringing Richard's bag back.

107
00:05:24,930 --> 00:05:25,930
Maybe.

108
00:05:25,930 --> 00:05:26,930
You're welcome anytime.

109
00:05:26,930 --> 00:05:29,930
Good-bye.

110
00:05:29,930 --> 00:05:36,930
Can I drive you home?

111
00:05:36,930 --> 00:05:37,930
No, thanks.

112
00:05:37,930 --> 00:05:38,930
The train is just up the street.

113
00:05:38,930 --> 00:05:39,930
It won't take me long at all.

114
00:05:39,930 --> 00:05:42,930
Well, you really saved the day for me, Alexandra.

115
00:05:42,930 --> 00:05:44,930
Bye.

116
00:05:44,930 --> 00:05:45,930
Bye-bye.

117
00:05:45,930 --> 00:05:46,930
Good night.

118
00:05:46,930 --> 00:05:57,930
She's a smart young lady, and very nice.

119
00:05:57,930 --> 00:06:01,930
Very! Hey, she forgot her bag!

120
00:06:01,930 --> 00:06:04,930
I guess we'll be seeing Alexandra again.

121
00:06:04,930 --> 00:06:07,930
Right, Robbie?
